      "math_academy_id": "e-13365",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14128904/assets/cecfcbd7a71796514dce5f79350800276155c2a9e52bd0eab1089ffdf1e66b04.svg)\n\nfind $P(2\\leq X \\leq 6).$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 6) & =P(2<X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(6)-F(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}-25}{75}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{75}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
